      <span class="eyebrow">About Triphala Powder</span>
      <h2 class="h-sec">What is Triphala <span class="it" style="color:var(--c)">powder?</span></h2>
      <p>Triphala means “three fruits” in Sanskrit. It is a traditional Ayurvedic blend of Amalaki (<i>Phyllanthus emblica</i>, Indian gooseberry), Haritaki (<i>Terminalia chebula</i>) and Bibhitaki (<i>Terminalia bellirica</i>), dried and milled together. It is one of the most widely used formulations in Ayurveda and is traditionally taken with warm water in the evening.</p><p>Veda Apothecary Triphala Powder is a pure three-fruit blend: only the three fruits, with no additives, fillers or preservatives. Its taste is tangy, slightly bitter and astringent — that is simply the natural flavor of the fruits, and nothing is added to mask it. Each fruit is listed individually on the Supplement Facts panel, as U.S. labeling requires for a blend.</p>
      <table class="facts"><caption class="sr-only">Triphala Powder key facts</caption><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Blend</th><td>Amalaki (<i>Phyllanthus emblica</i>), Haritaki (<i>Terminalia chebula</i>), Bibhitaki (<i>Terminalia bellirica</i>)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Plant part</th><td>Three fruits</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Net weight</th><td>8 oz (227 g)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Servings per container</th><td>about 38</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Ingredients</th><td>One — three fruits powder only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Origin</th><td>Product of India</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Distributed by</th><td>Old Soul Goods Inc.</td></tr></tbody></table>
    </div>
  </section>

